{"type":"Feature","properties":{"kind":"port_limits","cargo":[],"osm":["relation/15635213","relation/15635238","way/1553106476","relation/21528799","way/1565750072"],"source":"Derived: the convex hull of this port's terminals from OpenStreetMap, grown by 200 m, then cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it (the sea within its coastline, rivers, docks and basins), with the terminals kept whole","licence":"ODbL-1.0","reviewed_at":"2026-11-23","clip":"water","note":"OpenStreetMap maps no port limits for Tokyo. These are the hull of the container terminals below, grown by 200 m and cut to the water OpenStreetMap maps inside it, with the terminals kept whole: the terminals and the water between Shinagawa, Oi, Aomi and the Central Breakwater. The land of Aomi, its berths included, and of Odaiba is left out. A scan of OpenStreetMap finds no schools, hospitals or places of worship inside. The area OpenStreetMap maps as the Shinagawa terminal takes in four apartment blocks at its north-west corner, so they are inside. The named places are district (chōme) labels and reclaimed-island outlines under the terminals, slivers of three more islands and of Odaiba at the edge, and the outlines OpenStreetMap gives Aomi 2 to 4, Ariake 4 and Daiba 1, which reach over the water inside though their land is outside."},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[139.770162,35.585547],[139.770065,35.585451],[139.770038,35.585471],[139.769985,35.585493],[139.769881,35.585507],[139.769833,35.585506],[139.769786,35.585493],[139.769744,35.585469],[139.768772,35.584569],[139.767931,35.585182],[139.767726,35.585188],[139.767663,35.585132],[139.767388,35.584924],[139.767254,35.584835],[139.767081,35.584751],[139.766751,35.584609],[139.76658,35.584545],[139.76654,35.584352],[139.766788,35.584183],[139.770933,35.581193],[139.770924,35.581184],[139.770927,35.581174],[139.772713,35.579897],[139.772872,35.579902],[139.774584,35.581478],[139.776549,35.58327],[139.776656,35.583349],[139.777871,35.5